Description: panvk/jm: write query availability after the batch instead of splitting it
 Ending a query closed the current batch first, which split render passes
 into many batches. Collect the availability addresses per batch and write
 them in a short batch right after it; flush them before query copy/reset.
Author: pocket-debs
Origin: https://github.com/masterxq/mesa-lisbon (branch lisbon/26.3)
Forwarded: no
License: MIT (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
